sf-i-ghost-name = Mnemonic Ghost
sf-i-ghost-description = Reconnaissance infantry; detects cloaked targets within three cells. Fragile under focus fire. Exclusive to Echo Directorate.
sf-i-lance-name = Needle Chassis
sf-i-lance-description = Mobile precision gun. Long reload and low armor demand a screen. Exclusive to Echo Directorate.
sf-i-endurer-name = Endurer
sf-i-endurer-description = Expensive armored infantry; powerful in sustained exchanges but easily outmaneuvered. Exclusive to Iron Calculus.
sf-i-crucible-name = Crucible Engine
sf-i-crucible-description = Slow siege chassis with exceptional health and high replacement cost. Exclusive to Iron Calculus.
sf-i-thread-name = Threadkeeper
sf-i-thread-description = Anti-armor network infantry. Escort a relay rather than fighting alone. Exclusive to Custodian Grid.
sf-i-relay-name = Relay Walker
sf-i-relay-description = Four-cell command relay. Killing it removes the Grid formation advantage. Exclusive to Custodian Grid.
sf-i-savant-name = Circuit Savant
sf-i-savant-description = Fast experimental infantry; fragile but dangerous in short exchanges. Exclusive to Paradox Collegium.
sf-i-gambit-name = Gambit Rover
sf-i-gambit-description = Fast harassment vehicle; withdraw wounded survivors rather than trading with tanks. Exclusive to Paradox Collegium.
sf-f-regent-name = Uncrowned Regent
sf-f-regent-description = Armored fallen noble. Slow, costly infantry built to hold a position. Exclusive to Ashen Thrones.
sf-f-reliquary-name = Walking Reliquary
sf-f-reliquary-description = Bone-bound siege abomination; vulnerable while repositioning. Exclusive to Ashen Thrones.
sf-f-canticle-name = Mute Canticle
sf-f-canticle-description = Cheap ranged procession infantry; needs a Lamentor to reach full damage. Exclusive to Hollow Choir.
sf-f-lamentor-name = Lamentor
sf-f-lamentor-description = Four-cell profane hymn relay. The hymn amplifies damage dealt and received. Exclusive to Hollow Choir.
sf-f-flayer-name = Vow Flayer
sf-f-flayer-description = Fast melee infantry that becomes more dangerous when wounded; kite it. Exclusive to Carrion Testament.
sf-f-martyr-name = Carrion Martyr
sf-f-martyr-description = Melee abomination with a lethal wounded phase; lacks a ranged attack. Exclusive to Carrion Testament.
sf-f-pinions-name = Severed Pinion
sf-f-pinions-description = Grounded hunter with shattered wings; split from the army to gain range and speed. Exclusive to Broken Firmament.
sf-f-harrow-name = Harrow Stalker
sf-f-harrow-description = Independent flanking hunter. Clumping removes its isolation bonus. Exclusive to Broken Firmament.
sf-faction-i-echo-name = Echo Directorate
sf-faction-i-echo-description = Noetic Assembly: Patient reconnaissance and precision. After three seconds stationary, combat units gain 30% damage and 15% range.
sf-faction-i-iron-name = Iron Calculus
sf-faction-i-iron-description = Noetic Assembly: Armored attrition. Combat units take 20% less damage but move 15% slower.
sf-faction-i-grid-name = Custodian Grid
sf-faction-i-grid-description = Noetic Assembly: Network formations. Within four cells of a Relay Walker, combat units reload 20% faster and take 10% less damage.
sf-faction-i-paradox-name = Paradox Collegium
sf-faction-i-paradox-description = Noetic Assembly: Experimental skirmishers. Below half health, combat units move 30% faster and reload 15% faster; avoid sustained trades.
sf-faction-f-thrones-name = Ashen Thrones
sf-faction-f-thrones-description = Forsaken Host: Fallen aristocrats. After four seconds stationary, combat units take 30% less damage but attack 15% slower.
sf-faction-f-choir-name = Hollow Choir
sf-faction-f-choir-description = Forsaken Host: Corrupted procession. Within four cells of a Lamentor, combat units deal 25% more damage but take 10% more damage.
sf-faction-f-scars-name = Carrion Testament
sf-faction-f-scars-description = Forsaken Host: Wounded berserkers. Below half health, combat units deal 40% more damage and move 15% faster.
sf-faction-f-wings-name = Broken Firmament
sf-faction-f-wings-description = Forsaken Host: Isolated hunters. With no other friendly combat unit within four cells, gain 25% speed and 20% range.
